# Package Management Rules

## Package Manager
- Use pnpm as the primary package manager
- Maintain pnpm-lock.yaml for dependency locking
- Use pnpm workspaces for monorepos
- Run `pnpm install` for dependency installation
- Use `pnpm add` for adding new packages
- Use `pnpm remove` for removing packages
- Use `pnpm update` for updating packages

## Dependencies
- Keep dependencies up to date
- Use exact versions in package.json
- Audit dependencies regularly
- Use peerDependencies appropriately
- Minimize dependency size
- Use devDependencies for development tools

## Scripts
- Use pnpm run for script execution
- Maintain consistent script naming
- Document scripts in README.md
- Use cross-platform compatible commands
- Implement proper build scripts
- Use proper test scripts

## Best Practices
- Use .npmrc for pnpm configuration
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use proper CI/CD integration
- Keep node_modules in .gitignore
- Use proper version constraints
- Document dependency purposes 